@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Hi02 live render after PBR uniform alignment (2026-10-20)
+
+The current Release apphost was launched with the `asteroid-renderer-current-qa-20261020` 14-package NAP snapshot. `nexus-pack verify-active` passed immediately before launch. Its `asteroid-profile` package and active-manifest entry both declare content version 4. The application root had no loose `DATA` or `data` directory; every NAP archive came from `Data/NAP/`.
+
+The run used the current Release output, the full Surface profile, normal maps, metallic/roughness maps, environment maps, generated tangents, HDR, dynamic lighting and sun ambient. It started with `--new-game --invulnerable=on`, entered Hi02, read back a 640x480 frame and saved a 300-frame profile. The apphost ran with the installed .NET 10 runtime under SDL3 offscreen and Mesa OpenGL 4.3 (`NVE7`, Nouveau).
+
+The captured scene is a live-render smoke check after the PBR uniform layout correction. It shows the renderer reaching and drawing the system without a renderer exception. The 300-frame capture measured update plus draw at p50 95.729 ms, p95 138.686 ms and p99 143.847 ms on the old `NVE7`/Nouveau test GPU; these are host-specific measurements, not an RTX baseline or a controlled before/after result. The image does not identify a specific mapped PBR material, so it is not a material-by-material visual acceptance test. The process was stopped with SIGINT after the screenshot and profile were written. This run's valid active snapshot also does not reproduce the earlier `asteroid-profile` version-mismatch error from the `illum-detail-hdr-20261019` path; its current manifest contains `planet-hdr-profile`, not `asteroid-profile`.
+
+![Hi02 live scene with full Surface profile and HDR](hi02-pbr-uniform.png)
+
+Artifacts: [active NAP manifest](active.json), [300-frame profile](frame-profile.csv), and [runtime log](runtime.log.txt).
